1
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:04,920
Hi!

2
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:06,570
- Hey! - Hi!

3
00:00:07,070 --> 00:00:10,260
- How was the honeymoon? - Oh, incredible!

4
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:13,230
Champagne, candle-lit dinners,

5
00:00:13,280 --> 00:00:14,920
moonlight walks on the beach.

6
00:00:14,970 --> 00:00:16,730
It was so romantic.

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:18,900
- Where's Mike? - He's at the doctor.

8
00:00:18,950 --> 00:00:20,850
He didn't poop while we were there.

9
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,450
I'm glad you're back. I need your help.

10
00:00:25,450 --> 00:00:26,540
Oh, why, what's up?

11
00:00:26,590 --> 00:00:27,920
I have an audition for this play,

12
00:00:27,970 --> 00:00:29,950
and I have to speak French...

13
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:31,380
...which, according to my resume,

14
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:32,640
I'm fluent in.

15
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,930
Joey, you shouldn't lie on your resume.

16
00:00:35,980 --> 00:00:37,860
Yeah, you really shouldn't.

17
00:00:37,910 --> 00:00:38,470
By the way,

18
00:00:38,520 --> 00:00:40,750
how was that yearlong dig in Cairo?

19
00:00:42,530 --> 00:00:43,840
It was okay.

20
00:00:45,490 --> 00:00:47,350
I did not know you spoke French.

21
00:00:51,810 --> 00:00:53,330
You're so sexy.

22
00:00:54,350 --> 00:00:55,280
Well, so will you help me?

23
00:00:55,330 --> 00:00:56,330
I really wanna be in this play.

24
00:00:56,380 --> 00:00:57,080
Sure.

25
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:00,880
Seriously, stop it.

26
00:01:00,930 --> 00:01:01,940
I'm gonna jump on you.

27
00:01:03,790 --> 00:01:05,930
Friends S10E13 The One Where Joey Speaks French

28
00:01:44,590 --> 00:01:45,300
- Hey. - Hi.

29
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:47,090
Why are you wearing my apron?

30
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,340
I'm making cookies for Erica.

31
00:01:50,390 --> 00:01:52,230
We have to leave soon.

32
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:53,430
Her plane comes in in about an hour.

33
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:54,580
When she gets here,

34
00:01:54,630 --> 00:01:57,100
is it okay if I introduce you two as my wife...

35
00:01:57,150 --> 00:01:59,470
...and the woman who's carrying my child?

36
00:02:01,090 --> 00:02:01,930
No?

37
00:02:03,110 --> 00:02:04,080
Divorce?

38
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:07,510
- Hey. - Hey.

39
00:02:07,560 --> 00:02:09,320
You know where Rachel is?

40
00:02:09,370 --> 00:02:10,610
No, we haven't haven't seen her since morning.

41
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,820
It's unbelievable.

42
00:02:11,870 --> 00:02:12,710
She was supposed to meet me

43
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,180
a half-hour ago with Emma.

44
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:15,890
- Hey! - Hey!

45
00:02:15,940 --> 00:02:17,380
These are for Erica!

46
00:02:17,430 --> 00:02:19,220
She's gonna eat all those cookies?

47
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:21,200
Well, I want the baby to come out

48
00:02:21,250 --> 00:02:22,680
all cute and fat!

49
00:02:25,120 --> 00:02:26,880
So why is Erica coming to visit?

50
00:02:26,930 --> 00:02:28,510
We wanna get to know her better.

51
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:30,130
And she's never been to New York,

52
00:02:30,180 --> 00:02:31,940
so she wants to see the tourist spots:

53
00:02:31,990 --> 00:02:34,060
Statue of Liberty, Empire State Building.

54
00:02:34,110 --> 00:02:36,030
Oh, those places! There's always so many people,

55
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:38,330
and they're being corralled like cattle.

56
00:02:38,380 --> 00:02:42,050
And, you know, there's always some idiot who goes, "Moo."

57
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:44,650
Well, if it annoys you so much,

58
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:46,050
then why do you do it?

59
00:02:48,440 --> 00:02:50,750
Oh, hi. Hi. Thanks for showing up

60
00:02:50,750 --> 00:02:51,640
30 minutes late.

61
00:02:51,690 --> 00:02:52,240
Ross.

62
00:02:52,290 --> 00:02:54,290
No, I'm sure you have a great excuse.

63
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,780
What was it, a hair appointment?

64
00:02:55,830 --> 00:02:57,260
A mani-pedi?

65
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:59,050
Was there a sale at Barneys?{

66
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:01,920
My father had a heart attack.

67
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:04,410
While I was at Barneys.

68
00:03:07,380 --> 00:03:09,160
- Oh, my God, Rach. - Honey?

69
00:03:09,210 --> 00:03:11,790
- I'm so sorry. - Is he okay?

70
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:13,290
Yeah, he's gonna be fine,

71
00:03:13,340 --> 00:03:14,680
but he's heavily sedated.

72
00:03:14,730 --> 00:03:16,890
Okay, I'm gonna go to Long lsland with you.

73
00:03:16,940 --> 00:03:18,490
I mean, you can't be alone right now.

74
00:03:18,540 --> 00:03:21,350
No, come on, I'm totally okay.

75
00:03:21,660 --> 00:03:23,560
I don't need you to come.

76
00:03:24,130 --> 00:03:26,300
I can totally handle this on my own.

77
00:03:26,350 --> 00:03:29,290
Still, still, let me come for me.

78
00:03:30,390 --> 00:03:32,900
Okay. If you really need to.

79
00:03:33,500 --> 00:03:34,730
I bet someone could use

80
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:36,860
one of Monica's freshly baked cookies.

81
00:03:36,910 --> 00:03:38,200
Oh, I really could.

82
00:03:46,530 --> 00:03:48,500
All right, it seems pretty simple.

83
00:03:48,550 --> 00:03:50,820
Your first line is, "My name is Claude."

84
00:03:50,870 --> 00:03:52,820
So just repeat after me.

85
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,150
- Well, let's try it again. - Okay.

86
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,680
It's not...

87
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:14,040
...quite what I'm saying.

88
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:17,910
Really? Sounds exactly the same to me.

89
00:04:18,690 --> 00:04:20,520
- It does, really? - Yeah.

90
00:04:21,290 --> 00:04:22,830
- Let's just try it again. - Okay.

91
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,770
- Really listen. - Got it.

92
00:04:36,910 --> 00:04:39,400
- Hey, you guys! - Hi.

93
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:41,820
I want you to meet someone really special.

94
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:45,470
Phoebe, this is Erica. And this is the baby!

95
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:48,570
- Joey, Erica, baby. - Hi.

96
00:04:48,900 --> 00:04:51,470
Everyone, Erica! Baby!

97
00:04:52,050 --> 00:04:53,940
Monica. Calm. Self.

98
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:56,660
- Hey, sit down. - Thank you.

99
00:04:56,710 --> 00:04:58,210
It's really nice to meet you guys.

100
00:04:58,260 --> 00:04:59,740
I can't believe I'm here.

101
00:04:59,790 --> 00:05:02,250
Well, welcome to New York City, or should I say:

102
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:04,090

103
00:05:06,470 --> 00:05:07,940
Why would you say that?

104
00:05:09,390 --> 00:05:11,540
Okay. What are you gonna be doing today?

105
00:05:11,590 --> 00:05:13,330
Well, I wanna see everything!

106
00:05:13,380 --> 00:05:16,540
Times Square, Coney lsland, Rockefeller Center.

107
00:05:16,590 --> 00:05:17,580
Oh, you know what you should do?

108
00:05:17,630 --> 00:05:18,620
You should walk to

109
00:05:18,670 --> 00:05:19,900
the top of the Statue of Liberty.

110
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:22,680
- Oh, yeah, let's do that. - Great.

111
00:05:23,140 --> 00:05:25,140
This baby better be really good.

112
00:05:31,030 --> 00:05:32,440
Hi. Excuse me,

113
00:05:32,490 --> 00:05:33,360
I'm here to see my father.

114
00:05:33,410 --> 00:05:34,280
My name is Rachel Green.

115
00:05:34,330 --> 00:05:35,670
And I'm Dr. Ross Geller.

116
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,700
Ross, please, this is a hospital.

117
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:39,740
That actually means something here.

118
00:05:40,450 --> 00:05:42,590
- So can we please go in? - Absolutely.

119
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:44,840
Rach, I think I'm gonna wait out here...

120
00:05:44,890 --> 00:05:47,440
...because my throat is feeling a little scratchy.

121
00:05:47,490 --> 00:05:48,790
I don't wanna infect him.

122
00:05:48,840 --> 00:05:50,800
Ross, please. Don't be so scared of him.

123
00:05:50,850 --> 00:05:53,430
I am not scared of him. I'm really sick.

124
00:05:53,480 --> 00:05:54,420
He's under sedation,

125
00:05:54,470 --> 00:05:55,510
so he's pretty much out.

126
00:05:55,560 --> 00:05:56,700
I'm feeling better.

127
00:06:00,350 --> 00:06:02,080
Oh, my God.

128
00:06:04,400 --> 00:06:06,990
That ear and nose hair trimmer I got him

129
00:06:07,040 --> 00:06:08,950
was just money down the drain, huh?

130
00:06:10,350 --> 00:06:11,490
Ms. Green?

131
00:06:11,630 --> 00:06:13,080
Your father's doctor's on the phone

132
00:06:13,130 --> 00:06:14,180
if you'd like to speak to him.

133
00:06:14,230 --> 00:06:15,760
Oh, great. Are you gonna be okay?

134
00:06:15,930 --> 00:06:18,030
He's unconscious. We'll be just fine.

135
00:06:18,080 --> 00:06:18,710
Okay.

136
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:59,140
- Did the TV wake you? - No.

137
00:06:59,610 --> 00:07:01,770
When you put your feet up on my bed,

138
00:07:01,820 --> 00:07:03,680
you tugged on my catheter.

139
00:07:10,860 --> 00:07:12,600
What are you doing here, Geller?

140
00:07:12,650 --> 00:07:13,850
Well, I came with Rachel,

141
00:07:13,900 --> 00:07:15,720
who should be back any second.

142
00:07:16,880 --> 00:07:18,070
So, what's new?

143
00:07:18,340 --> 00:07:20,300
Oh, I had a little heart attack.

144
00:07:21,250 --> 00:07:22,850
Right. Is it painful?

145
00:07:23,090 --> 00:07:24,170
What, the heart attack

146
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,490
or sitting here talking to you?

147
00:07:27,490 --> 00:07:30,350
Let's see if we can get that Rachel back in here.

148
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:32,450
So, what's new with you?

149
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,730
Knocked up any more of my daughters lately?

150
00:07:34,780 --> 00:07:36,940
Nope. Just the one. Rach!

151
00:07:43,350 --> 00:07:44,480
No!

152
00:07:45,540 --> 00:07:48,060
Okay, maybe if we just break it down.

153
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:51,480
Okay, let's try it one syllable at a time.

154
00:07:51,530 --> 00:07:53,220
Okay, so repeat after me.

155
00:07:57,680 --> 00:07:59,090
Great! Okay, faster.

156
00:08:07,070 --> 00:08:09,470
Okay, it's too hard. I can't teach you.

157
00:08:09,470 --> 00:08:10,090
What are you doing?

158
00:08:10,140 --> 00:08:11,070
I have to go

159
00:08:11,120 --> 00:08:12,550
before I put your head through a wall.

160
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:15,040
Don't go, I need you!

161
00:08:15,090 --> 00:08:16,710
My audition is tomorrow!

162
00:08:33,410 --> 00:08:35,970
Hey. I was gonna make us some dinner...

163
00:08:36,020 --> 00:08:37,600
...but all I found in your dad's fridge

164
00:08:37,650 --> 00:08:39,360
was bacon and heavy cream.

165
00:08:40,690 --> 00:08:41,490
I think we solved

166
00:08:41,540 --> 00:08:42,970
the mystery of the heart attack.

167
00:08:43,420 --> 00:08:44,780
Did you call your parents?

168
00:08:44,830 --> 00:08:46,160
Oh, yeah. Emma's doing great.

169
00:08:46,210 --> 00:08:47,380
Oh, good.

170
00:08:50,790 --> 00:08:52,930
- What? - I just can't believe...

171
00:08:52,980 --> 00:08:54,720
...I'm in Rachel Green's room.

172
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:56,670
What do you mean?

173
00:08:56,720 --> 00:08:58,270
You've been in my room before.

174
00:08:58,440 --> 00:09:00,050
Yeah, sure, right.

175
00:09:01,390 --> 00:09:03,580
Like I'd ever be in Rachel Green's room.

176
00:09:03,630 --> 00:09:04,830
Okay, I gotta tell you,

177
00:09:04,880 --> 00:09:06,590
it's really weird when you use my whole name.

178
00:09:07,630 --> 00:09:08,610
Sorry.

179
00:09:10,610 --> 00:09:12,620
- You okay? - Yeah.

180
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:15,010
- Yeah, you had a rough day. - Yeah.

181
00:09:15,060 --> 00:09:17,820
It's just so weird seeing him like that, you know?

182
00:09:17,870 --> 00:09:19,380
I mean, he's a doctor.

183
00:09:19,430 --> 00:09:22,150
You don't expect doctors to get sick.

184
00:09:22,560 --> 00:09:23,980
But we do.

185
00:09:28,660 --> 00:09:30,470
He's gonna be okay, Rach.

186
00:09:35,220 --> 00:09:36,790
I don't want him to wake up alone.

187
00:09:36,840 --> 00:09:37,980
I should go to the hospital.

188
00:09:38,030 --> 00:09:39,920
What? No, no. Hey, hey, look.

189
00:09:39,970 --> 00:09:40,430
What?

190
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:42,100
They gave him a lot of medication.

191
00:09:42,150 --> 00:09:44,070
He wouldn't even know if you were there.

192
00:09:44,120 --> 00:09:46,630
We'll go see him first thing in the morning. Ok?

193
00:09:46,680 --> 00:09:48,080
Really? I shouldn't feel guilty?

194
00:09:48,130 --> 00:09:49,080
No-- God, hey.

195
00:09:49,130 --> 00:09:51,600
Rach, you've been an amazing daughter, okay?

196
00:09:51,650 --> 00:09:53,620
Right now you need to get some rest.

197
00:09:53,630 --> 00:09:55,100
Okay, maybe you're right.

198
00:09:55,970 --> 00:09:57,110
Good night.

199
00:09:59,370 --> 00:10:00,800
Wait, wait, wait.

200
00:10:02,030 --> 00:10:03,390
Would you stay here

201
00:10:03,440 --> 00:10:04,900
with me for a little while?

202
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:07,810
- Sure. - Okay.

203
00:10:09,370 --> 00:10:11,720
Thank you for coming with me today.

204
00:10:11,770 --> 00:10:13,140
Oh, of course.

205
00:10:13,190 --> 00:10:15,830
Rachel Green is very happy you're in her room.

206
00:10:17,760 --> 00:10:19,820
Me too. Come here.

207
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:24,160
I just don't wanna be alone tonight.

208
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:26,340
Okay, well,

209
00:10:26,590 --> 00:10:29,620
I can maybe grab a sleeping bag or--

210
00:10:44,970 --> 00:10:46,370
No, Rach!

211
00:10:47,700 --> 00:10:48,540
I'm sorry,

212
00:10:48,590 --> 00:10:51,650
I just don't think this is a good idea.

213
00:10:51,700 --> 00:10:53,900
Well, we won't know that until we do it,

214
00:10:53,950 --> 00:10:54,800
will we?

215
00:10:54,850 --> 00:10:56,470
No, look, uh.

216
00:10:57,210 --> 00:11:00,060
You are upset about your father,

217
00:11:00,110 --> 00:11:01,700
and you're feeling vulnerable...

218
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:03,370
...and I just don't feel it

219
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:04,170
would be right.

220
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:05,540
I feel like I'd be, you know,

221
00:11:05,590 --> 00:11:06,700
taking advantage of you.

222
00:11:06,750 --> 00:11:07,820
What--? Taking advantage?

223
00:11:07,870 --> 00:11:10,760
I am giving you the advantage. Enjoy!

224
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:14,870
Look, I'm sure it would be great...

225
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:18,230
...but I think one of us has to be thinking clearly.

226
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:20,210
So I'm gonna go.

227
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:27,120
Okay.

228
00:11:31,090 --> 00:11:32,730
I'll see you in the morning.

229
00:11:36,060 --> 00:11:37,520
I haven't had sex in four months.

230
00:11:37,570 --> 00:11:39,150
I should get a medal for that!

231
00:11:46,100 --> 00:11:48,450
Thanks so much for taking me to all those places.

232
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,510
I had a great time.

233
00:11:49,560 --> 00:11:50,460
I'm glad.

234
00:11:50,510 --> 00:11:52,430
Listen, I wanna apologize about Chandler, though.

235
00:11:52,480 --> 00:11:54,300
I just did not see this coming.

236
00:11:54,350 --> 00:11:56,560
New York is awesome!

237
00:11:59,150 --> 00:12:00,360
What is with you?

238
00:12:00,410 --> 00:12:02,300
You know, I've been to these places before...

239
00:12:02,350 --> 00:12:04,010
...but I've never really seen them.

240
00:12:04,060 --> 00:12:05,910
Yeah, you miss a lot when you're mooing.

241
00:12:08,060 --> 00:12:10,060
Thank you for showing me around.

242
00:12:10,110 --> 00:12:11,620
Oh, it was our pleasure.

243
00:12:11,670 --> 00:12:13,770
We're so much enjoying getting to know you.

244
00:12:13,970 --> 00:12:16,380
Well, if there's anything else you wanna know....

245
00:12:19,580 --> 00:12:20,740
Okay.

246
00:12:22,090 --> 00:12:23,240
Can we ask you some questions

247
00:12:23,290 --> 00:12:24,480
about the father?

248
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:26,460
Oh, sure. Yeah.

249
00:12:26,910 --> 00:12:29,040
Well, he was my high-school boyfriend,

250
00:12:29,090 --> 00:12:31,440
captain of the football team, really cute.

251
00:12:32,100 --> 00:12:34,460
Got a scholarship and went to college.

252
00:12:34,510 --> 00:12:35,570
That's great.

253
00:12:36,790 --> 00:12:39,510
Yeah, it's almost definitely him.

254
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:43,030
How's that, now?

255
00:12:43,690 --> 00:12:46,300
Well, there's a chance it's another guy.

256
00:12:46,600 --> 00:12:49,760
I mean, I've only ever been with two guys...

257
00:12:50,350 --> 00:12:52,130
...but they sort of overlapped.

258
00:12:53,300 --> 00:12:54,950
So, what does the other guy do?

259
00:12:55,000 --> 00:12:56,480
Does he go to college too?

260
00:12:56,530 --> 00:12:57,910
No, he's in prison.

261
00:13:00,780 --> 00:13:03,720
Was he falsely accused of something?

262
00:13:05,080 --> 00:13:06,510
No.

263
00:13:06,780 --> 00:13:08,970
He killed his father with a shovel.

264
00:13:11,120 --> 00:13:13,070
Other than that, he's a great guy.

265
00:13:13,120 --> 00:13:15,420
I'll bet his dad doesn't think so.

266
00:13:24,920 --> 00:13:27,180
- Are you awake? - Of course I'm awake.

267
00:13:27,230 --> 00:13:29,390
Assume from now on that I'm always awake.

268
00:13:31,520 --> 00:13:34,020
All right, we don't know that it's him.

269
00:13:34,070 --> 00:13:35,540
I mean, it could be the football guy.

270
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:36,720
Honey, it's us.

271
00:13:36,770 --> 00:13:38,570
Of course it's the shovel killer.

272
00:13:43,270 --> 00:13:45,420
Well, all right, let's say that it is him.

273
00:13:45,470 --> 00:13:47,380
Would we not want the baby? No.

